date-released: 2026-10-14
repository-code: "https://github.com/gromfy01/wire-drawing-pinn-surrogates"
abstract: >-
  Code, run log and verification scripts behind the paper "Physics-informed versus
  data-driven surrogates for residual stress after wire drawing: accuracy, physical
  admissibility and behaviour outside the training range". Starting from the raw Abaqus
  reports of 2443 axisymmetric finite-element simulations of single-pass drawing of
  AISI 1020 steel wire, the code rebuilds the two datasets of the paper (1756 cases each),
  reruns the matrix of 341 training runs that compares a multilayer perceptron, a
  strong-form physics-informed network and a weak-form variational physics-informed
  network, regenerates the result tables and field figures, and reproduces the
  drawing-stress verification on 112 simulations. The finite-element data are deposited
  in a separate Zenodo record.
keywords:
  - physics-informed neural networks
  - surrogate models
  - wire drawing
  - residual stress
  - finite element method
